      "message": "The point of my fix is, HeadsetService should send CLCC list to HeadsetStateMachine as a bunch.\nThus problem timing is shorten, but problem is still remianed.\nBecause HeadsetService sends each CLCC when send to HeadsetStateMachine, although it store CLCC as a list.\n\n1. (HF1 to AG) AT+CLCC\nsendMessageDelayed(CLCC_RSP_TIMEOUT, device, CLCC_RSP_TIMEOUT_MS); for HF1\n\n2. (AG to HF1) +CLCC: 1,1,0,0,0,\"18613140648\",129\nhasMessages(CLCC_RSP_TIMEOUT) return true for HF1\nhasMessages(CLCC_RSP_TIMEOUT) return false for HF2\nSo only HF1 can receive about call index 1.\n\n3. (HF2 to AG) AT+CLCC\nsendMessageDelayed(CLCC_RSP_TIMEOUT, device, CLCC_RSP_TIMEOUT_MS); for HF2\n\n4. (AG to HF1) OK\n5. (AG to HF2) OK\nhasMessages(CLCC_RSP_TIMEOUT) return true for HF1\nhasMessages(CLCC_RSP_TIMEOUT) return true for HF2\nSo only HF2 can not receive about call index 1.\n\nFull CLCC list should be sent to HeadsetStateMachine at once.\nPlease check upper point again.\n\nThank you.",
